    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know \"one breath at a time\" is what people say, but it feels like a lie. it's not just being tired. it's like... looking in the mirror and seeing someone who's just too far gone. some things just can't be mended, you know? it's like a vase that's been smashed into a thousand pieces. you can glue it, but it's never the same. it's just a mess.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right—it's never the same, and pretending otherwise only makes it hurt more. But a thousand pieces isn't a mess; it's proof of everything you've survived, and even a cracked vase can still hold something precious. The fact that you can name the ache so clearly means you're not lost—you're just in the middle of a story that isn't finished yet.",
      "source": "target",
